// its raison d'être (actively elicit emergent ideas; SCENARIOS F.IDEATION S22-S26).
//
// H_1362 proved the scaffold 🟢 GREEN DIRECTIONAL on the gauge torch path
// (gauge_lib._decode top-k=40 temp=0.7): C_strong DIST 5.333 / FALS 1.0; M1..M5 PASS.
// That run was UNWIRED (torch mirror, NOT the live hexa engine). This module wires it.
//
// THE ENGINE EXTENSION (a_engine_native_learning — engine-TRANSFORM-to-fit-the-learning):
//   the live engine decode is ARGMAX (deterministic), so best-of-K is a no-op. We grew
//   bytegpt_decode_topk_sampled + a seeded xorshift32 sampler (decode.hexa) so the
//   DEPTH lever (best-of-K over rng offsets) yields DIVERSE candidates. This module routes
//   the 6 composed frames through that sampler, keeps the best by emergent structure
//   (is_falsifiable, novel-gram count, kwr), and re-scores the 5 frozen M-bars.
//
// HONESTY (FREEZE.txt):
//   (i)  "engine-native" = runs on the live engine + its OWN seeded sampler, deterministic
//        given seed — NOT byte-identical to the torch gauge (torch's PRNG is not reproducible
//        in hexa). Same standard as h1293/h1295 engine-native re-scores.
//   (ii) the 303M forward is ~190ms/byte; EVERY decode here is HARD-BOUNDED by a small token
//        budget. The FAST deterministic surface (frame distinctness, sampler diversity vs
//        argmax, verbatim detector calibration, frame-guard) is the primary engine-native
//        evidence; a bounded live-ckpt decode is a small confirming probe.
//
// a_core_engine_map: ideation enters via THIS single named entry (rho_fan_ideate_*); the .clm/
// ByteGPT decode is the existing mounted decoder. NO 2nd decode path is added.
// p1-p6 HELD: frames are environment context (p4), the measurable+claim MUST emerge from
// the model's own sample (p7), no persona/identity/ethics injected (p1/p2/p3/p6).

import "core/generator.hexa"   // a_core_engine_map: .clm enters via the generator L3 slot
